{
  "notes": "Cinematic, B harmonic minor, 86 BPM. A colony on another world: a granular flute cloud pitched up an octave holding each chord's third and fifth (a high, glassy whistle in the air), a gliding FM bass in a lopsided 3+3+3+3+2+2 sixteenth grouping, the player's synthetic voice on the Smart Keys (TALKBOX: a vowel that turns on every note, glide, vibrato) through a fast triplet echo, and tribal drums: deep kick, congas and a cowbell ping. The Smart Keys play a five-note subset of the key, B C# D F# G (a hirajoshi colour), consonant over i, iv and VI; the augmented III+ (D F# A#) is the alien chord and always falls back to Bm by its leading tone. Scenes: A Bm and G over a B pedal; B the loop i VI iv III+ with the bass on the roots; C turns the loop around (iv VI III+ and the arrival on i) under a busier groove; D the augmented chord over the B pedal (the minor-major seventh) and home. ENERGY brings the bass, then the drums, then fills. All material is original.",
